.el .ds Aq '
.TH parsec-cli-server-stats 1  "stats " 
.SH NAME
parsec\-cli\-server\-stats \- Get a per\-organization report of server usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBparsec\-cli server stats\fR [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-end\-date\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-token\fR> <\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-addr\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get a per\-organization report of server usage
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Administration token
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPARSEC_ADMINISTRATION_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-addr\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Server address (e.g: parsec3://127.0.0.1:6770?no_ssl=true)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPARSEC_SERVER_ADDR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-end\-date\fR \fI<END_DATE>\fR
Ignore everything after this date (e.g: 2024\-01\-01T00:00:00\-00:00)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
